= render_in_modal do
  -# Visualization tab: the OntoPortal BioMixer Visualizer, embedded in an iframe
  -# (see visualizer_embed_url). It draws its own chrome and drives its own
  -# fullscreen through the Fullscreen API — which an iframe may only use when the
  -# embedder allows it — so `allow` replaces the resize glue the legacy BioMixer
  -# embed needed from the portal.
  .visualizer-embed
    %iframe{src: visualizer_embed_url(@ontology, @concept),
            title: t('concepts.visualization'),
            allow: 'fullscreen', allowfullscreen: true,
            frameborder: 0, width: '100%', height: '100%'}
